  "narrative": {
    "northStar":"Airy international MICE studio",
    "overview":"Light, airy and clean: large ink sans-serif typography sits on warm-white paper, with generous space and daylight imagery. The first view is now an asymmetric real-photo collage: magnolia in a Suzhou garden, a willow-lined canal boat and butterfly embroidery sit beside the left-aligned title and copy on desktop, then below that copy on mobile. Restrained mandarin accents bring energy and positivity. This records the implemented local draft; publication remains unresolved.",
    "keyCharacteristics":["Spacious, light composition.","Large, clear Manrope headings.","An asymmetric real-photo hero collage with garden, water and handwork.","Flat controls and unboxed editorial lists.","Small, purposeful mandarin accents."],
    "rules":[{"name":"The Restrained Accent Rule","body":"Keep mandarin in purposeful small elements: the main action, wordmark square and scope separator.","section":"colors"}],
    "dos":["Do use warm-white space, large ink Manrope headings and restrained mandarin accents.","Do keep the hero title and copy left of the collage on desktop, then above it on mobile.","Do keep the hero collage real-photo, asymmetric and limited to magnolia Suzhou garden, willow-lined canal boat and butterfly embroidery.","Do keep service descriptions unboxed and venue imagery unframed.","Do preserve visible keyboard focus and reduced-motion behavior."],
    "donts":["Don't introduce the rejected dark presentation or orange-dominant block layout.","Don't treat illustrative venue imagery as evidence of a completed project."]
